  "articleBody": "While small accent trim might look tempting as a weekend project, certain wall conditions call for experienced hands to avoid ruined materials and misaligned profiles. \n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nLook for these signs that indicate your project needs a professional finish contractor:\n- Walls are noticeably bowed, wavy, or out-of-plumb across long stretches.\n- Existing baseboards, crown molding, or door casings do not align with standard panel thicknesses.\n- Electrical boxes, vents, or heating registers sit right where panel rails or stiles must land.\n- The project covers large, interconnected spaces with multiple outside corners and staircases.\n- You are using delicate, high-end, or moisture-resistant custom materials that leave no room for cutting errors.\n\nGetting seamless results across uneven walls requires precise scribing, stud fastening, and careful trim integration. When electrical boxes need moving, partnering with a general contractor who handles framing, drywall, and trade coordination keeps the work compliant and smooth.\n\nIf your home presents tricky angles or extensive layout challenges, let an experienced contractor take over. Reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to discuss your interior wainscoting plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
